<pdd-reason>Fail-closed backend feature flag evaluator answering is_enabled from in-memory flag state.</pdd-reason>

<pdd-interface>
{
  "type": "module",
  "module": {
    "functions": [
      {"name": "is_enabled", "signature": "(flag_name: str, uid: str)", "returns": "bool"},
      {"name": "_set_flags", "signature": "(flags: dict[str, bool])", "returns": "None"}
    ]
  }
}
</pdd-interface>

<pdd-dependency>python_preamble.prompt</pdd-dependency>

<include optional>context/python_preamble.prompt</include>

% Goal
Provide a backend feature flag evaluator that answers `is_enabled(flag_name, uid) -> bool` from in-memory state, fail-closed on unknown or malformed input.

% Role & Scope
A small, dependency-free module at `src/feature_flags/evaluator.py`. Owns a module-level mapping of flag name to enabled state and exposes a single read API plus a test/loader seam for populating that state. The flag state is populated by a sibling config loader (out of scope here); this module does not import the loader and never raises on unknown flags.

% Public API
- `is_enabled(flag_name: str, uid: str) -> bool`
- `_set_flags(flags: dict[str, bool]) -> None` (test/loader seam)
- `_FLAGS: dict[str, bool]` (module-level state, initially empty)

% Requirements
1. `is_enabled(flag_name, uid)` returns `True` only when `flag_name` is a key in `_FLAGS` whose value is truthy; otherwise returns `False`.
2. Unknown flag names return `False` (never raise `KeyError`).
3. Non-string `flag_name` (e.g., `None`, int) returns `False` without raising.
4. `uid` is accepted in the signature for forward compatibility (per-user targeting in a future revision) but MUST NOT influence the result in this version.
5. The function never raises for any input combination; it is fail-closed.
6. `_set_flags(flags)` replaces the contents of `_FLAGS` atomically (clear + update) so callers see a consistent snapshot. It accepts a `dict[str, bool]`-like mapping and coerces each value to `bool`.
7. `_FLAGS` is a module-level `dict` initialized to empty; it is the single source of in-memory state. No singletons, classes, or globals beyond this dict.
8. No I/O, no logging side effects, no external dependencies — standard library only.
9. Include a docstring on `is_enabled` describing the fail-closed contract and that `uid` is reserved for future per-user evaluation.
10. Type-annotate the public API.

% Deliverables
- Code: `src/feature_flags/evaluator.py`
